== Demographics ==

[[File:Original street market.png|thumb|250px|A street market in the Barri Negre, Original's historic Black Balboan neighbourhood]]

=== Historical population ===

{{Historical populations|align=right|title=Historical population of Original|footnote=Figures prior to 1960 refer to the area corresponding to the modern ciutat boundaries.|1950=252,000|1960=498,000|1970=648,000|1980=583,000|1990=521,000|2000=598,000|2010=662,000|2020=714,000|2026=731,320}}

Original's population history reflects the city's successive transformations. The settlement that became Sant Cristòfor grew from a small Volisanian colonial outpost to a major port city: approximately 80,000 at independence in 1854, and over 200,000 by the 1880s. At that time, the entire city was essentially what is now Original — the outer ciutats had not yet developed. The Zong Balboa period saw explosive growth across the territory, but the core (now Original) grew more slowly as population spread into the new suburbs and exurbs. The pre-GAW peak is estimated at approximately 550,000.

The Great Adonian War devastated the population. Twelve years of siege caused widespread famine, disease, and displacement; by 1947, the population of the core had fallen to an estimated 180,000 — a loss of nearly two-thirds. The post-war return of displaced residents and the Second Star rebuilding pushed the population back to nearly 500,000 by 1960. The post-reunification period saw a second decline as families moved to the outer ciutats, bottoming out around 520,000 in the early 1990s. The urban renaissance of the 2000s — driven by gentrification, the financial sector, and the conversion of former docklands — brought steady repopulation, reaching 731,320 by 2026.

Original's population of 731,320 makes it the second-most populous ciutat in Sant Cristòfor. Its demographic profile differs significantly from the city-wide average: it has a higher proportion of Black Balboans (35.2% vs. 34.6% city-wide), reflecting the historic southern neighbourhoods, and a lower proportion of White Balboans (8.0% vs. 9.1%), who concentrate in [[Costa Nord (ciutat)|Costa Nord]] and [[Sant Miquel (ciutat)|Sant Miquel]]. The Zong (8.0%) and Nakamian (4.4%) communities are concentrated in the eastern barris and bay shore financial district.

